Interestingly, I didn’t mention finding this new journaling app or coding a new one. Instead, I simply asked the LLM to record me and store the recording in a markdown file within my existing file system, and it did exactly that. 

There was no new user interface, no new user experience, and no new app; it was simply the native LLM capabilities being utilized. Many software applications will likely be absorbed by LLMs. 

LLMs have the ability to make technology disappear, which is a delightful aspect from a user experience perspective.

